WEBVTT

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.490
Good outbound comes down to three things.

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:06.940
The right company. The right person.
And the right first line.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:12.510
The Personal GTM Engine does the research
and leaves the final call to a human.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.600
It runs in eight stages.
It discovers companies,

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:20.230
filters them with plain rules,
scores them, and enriches them.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.440
Then it finds the founder
and drafts a first message.

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:28.170
A human reviews every draft, and
approved work goes straight into HubSpot.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.950
The rule is simple.
No AI before the gates.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:36.340
In one run, 377 YC companies came in.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:43.140
Time zone, activity, and team size filters cut that
down to 23 before a single credit was spent.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:45.810
Only the survivors cost anything.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.420
A free website scan detects their CRM and tools.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.130
Clay adds a research summary and a dated trigger
for one credit per account.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:59.660
Founders come from the company's YC page,
accepted only when the domain matches,

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.720
and Clay's email waterfall verified 19 out of 20.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:08.740
Drafts are written by free models,
falling back from Groq to Gemini,

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.060
with a template as the last resort.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.650
Every draft passes a strict validator.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.420
No invented numbers.
Only tools seen on their site.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:20.230
And never pitching a company its own product.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.980
In the latest run, 8 of 8 passed.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:25.240
Then a human steps in.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:29.800
Every draft lands in a private review console
with the reasoning behind it.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.190
Why this person, and why now.

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:36.160
You approve, edit, or reject.
There's no send button.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.960
Messages go out by hand,
and every decision is logged.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:46.090
Once a draft is approved, the company, the contact,
and a deal are created in HubSpot.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:51.160
Deal stages sync back every 30 minutes,
and a second run writes nothing new.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.940
The whole stack runs on free tiers.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:57.780
n8n, Neon, Vercel, Clay, Groq, and HubSpot.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.300
Total cost: $0 a month.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.390
The results so far.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:07.800
49 accounts scored, 37 verified founder emails,
42 drafts, 7 deals in HubSpot,

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.680
and 0 messages sent without approval.

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:17.420
The Personal GTM Engine.
Built by Mohamed Landolsi.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:22.000
The code is on GitHub,
and there's more at mohamedlandolsi.tech.
